# BigCam: USB autosuspend and video capture.
#
# USB autosuspend makes some UVC webcams drop frames or take seconds to wake
# up.  BigCam handles this itself: StreamEngine._disable_usb_autosuspend()
# sets power/control to "on" for the camera in use and restores the previous
# value when the stream stops.
#
# The rule below used to do the same thing globally and permanently:
#
#   ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="video4linux", RUN+="/bin/sh -c 'echo on > ...'"
#
# That disabled autosuspend for *every* video device on the machine, for the
# whole session, whether or not BigCam was running — a measurable battery
# cost on laptops — and it spawned a shell on every device event.
#
# It is left disabled on purpose.  Uncomment only if your hardware needs
# autosuspend off before BigCam opens the device (rare; some hubs enumerate
# too slowly).  Prefer restricting it to the affected camera's VID:PID:
#
# ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTR{idVendor}=="046d", ATTR{idProduct}=="082d", \
#   TEST=="power/control", ATTR{power/control}="on"
